     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the total daily dose looks too high and I want to check it with you first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. The usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2550 mg/day, and for extended-release it's 2000 mg/day. Your order is about twice the IR maximum, which raises the risk of GI side effects and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney function.\n\n**Some possible intended orders:**\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum). This may be what you meant, since 1700 is 2 \u00d7 850.\n- **Metformin 1700 mg/day total in divided doses**, such as 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily** (2000 mg/day, a common target dose).\n\nLet me know which of these you meant, or give me the corrected dose and frequency. If you do mean 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and tell me the clinical reason. I'll enter it with a note documenting your confirmation."
      }
     ],
